# Print colours

Use these colours for printed material, such as a household guide, a label for a device or a sign by the boiler. For screens, use [Web-app colours](colour-web-app.html).

Each colour except White has a CMYK and a Pantone reference. White has neither. The values are references, not measured matches, so [check a printed proof](colour.html#bg-col-08) before you print many copies.

For example, a printed guide to the Morgan household's heating could use:

- Primary blue for the cover band and headings
- Black for body text and Black tint 25% for notes
- Blue tint 80% behind a box such as “If the boiler shows a fault”
- Primary red only beside the words “Turn off the gas supply”, so the warning does not depend on colour

